{:title
 "Archetypal Smile, the Answer to Whether Something Can Be Smile",
 :description
 "What Archetypal Smile is in THE MAP, the repository of every face that can be Smile, its parts, its anatomical order, every face smiling and the mouth deciding, and how my words reached that layer in August 2026, from a 2023 search for archetypal patterns of prompting, with every source.",
 :keywords
 "Archetypal Smile, emoticon anatomy, mouths eyes noses hats scarves, every face smiles, Smile version and archetype, prompt language design, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "In THE MAP, Archetypal Smile answers one question, can this be Smile? It keeps every face that can be Smile. Meaning belongs to a version, bounds belong to a version, and use belongs to a lens.",
 :paras
 ["THE MAP gives the archetype its parts, mouths, eyes, noses, and emphasis worn as hats and scarves, in an anatomical order that makes marks read as a face. Every face smiles, true in every version, and a face that frowns is recognised and refused by name. The mouth carries the smile, while noses and eyes are neutral on their own. Orientation is its own dimension, forward or mirrored, and a mirrored smile closes the closest face before it that matches its nesting. Greater size means more, and each mark brings the meaning it already has in ordinary writing. The archetype grows when a version needs something it cannot yet express."
 "The word archetypal is in my words of October 2023, a search for the archetypal patterns of prompting, followed in [[t:precursor-the-archetypal-patterns-of-prompting]]."
 "In July 2025 the faces arrived and were spoken of as beings, “how I use entities I'm like they're memorable interesting semantic characters that help you structure your prompt”.[[m:2025-07-03]] Their parts began to loosen, “For a long time I thought that you needed the kolons, the eyes, but you don't.”[[m:2025-07-24]] and “Smiles can have only eyes, only mouths, or both.”[[m:2025-07-31]]"
 "Archetypal Smile as THE MAP keeps it was defined between 1 and 15 August 2026, apart from any one version. On 1 August, “There is also no limit on mouth number in the archetypal language.”, “four space law is definitely not smile archetypal and is an implementation detail”, and the mirror kept so “All sad looking faces are not Smile.”[[m:2026-08-01]] On 4 August, “the archetypal smile updates when a new definition demands it, thats the cycle of growth”.[[m:2026-08-04]] On 5 August, “the archetypal always wants to be a repository of possibility”, and “yes the archtypal is all about if it can be smile”.[[m:2026-08-05]] On 12 August, “The mouth is what determines it as a smile.”[[m:2026-08-12]] The alphabet then grew by my additions, “3 is also a mouth eg :-3.”, sunglasses eyes, and a heart added and taken out again, “actually remove the heart. its not a smile.”[[m:2026-08-13]]"
 "In October I asked for sad emoticons “for when you need to indicate something has gone wrong”, while THE MAP keeps a frowning face recognised and refused by name.[[m:2026-10-14]]"
 "So my words moved from archetypal patterns of prompting in 2023, through faces as beings in 2025, to the possibility space of every face in August 2026. A version chooses from it, followed in [[t:version]], and the faces it chooses are the [[t:delimiter]]."],
 :faq
 [["What is Archetypal Smile?"
 "The layer of Smile that answers whether something can be Smile, keeping every face that smiles with its parts and their order, while each version gives particular faces their meanings and bounds."]
 ["What makes a face a smile?"
 "The mouth. Noses and eyes are neutral on their own, and the mouth's turn relative to the eyes is what smiles."]]}
